

We'll use:
- 1 Master node in the public subnet.
- 2 Worker nodes in the private subnet.
- kubeadm to initialize and join the cluster.
- containerd as the container runtime.
- Calico as the CNI network plugin.

How the communication works:
1. You connect to the master using SSH.
2. The master exposes Kubernetes API Server on port 6443.
3. Workers communicate with the master using its private IP.
4. Workers download packages through a NAT Gateway (or another configured outbound route).
5. You deploy applications to the workers.




2. Inbound Rules
Configure the following rules:
Type / Port	Protocol	Source	Purpose
SSH (22)	TCP	Your public IP /32	SSH access
Custom TCP (6443)	TCP	k8s-cluster-sg	Kubernetes API Server
Custom TCP (2379-2380)	TCP	k8s-cluster-sg	etcd
Custom TCP (10250)	TCP	k8s-cluster-sg	Kubelet API
Custom TCP (10257)	TCP	k8s-cluster-sg	Controller Manager
Custom TCP (10259)	TCP	k8s-cluster-sg	Scheduler
Custom TCP (30000-32767)	TCP	Required clients	NodePort services
Custom UDP (4789)	UDP	k8s-cluster-sg	Calico VXLAN (if enabled)


3. Outbound Rules
Allow all outbound traffic:
Type	Protocol	Port	Destination
All traffic	All	All	0.0.0.0/0
